# Radix Tooltip only

Every **product tooltip** (hover/focus hint on buttons, icons, toolbar controls, truncated labels, etc.) must use Radix **`Tooltip`** from `radix-ui` (or `@radix-ui/react-tooltip`).

Do **not** use native HTML `title=` as the tooltip UI. Do not invent custom hover divs or other tooltip libraries.

## Pattern

```tsx
import { Tooltip } from 'radix-ui';

<Tooltip.Provider delayDuration={250} skipDelayDuration={0}>
  <Tooltip.Root>
    <Tooltip.Trigger asChild>
      <button type="button" aria-label="닫기">
        …
      </button>
    </Tooltip.Trigger>
    <Tooltip.Portal>
      <Tooltip.Content
        side="top"
        sideOffset={6}
        className="z-100001 max-w-[min(92vw,280px)] rounded-md border …"
      >
        닫기
        <Tooltip.Arrow className="fill-white dark:fill-odp-surface" />
      </Tooltip.Content>
    </Tooltip.Portal>
  </Tooltip.Root>
</Tooltip.Provider>
```

Reuse an ancestor `Tooltip.Provider` when several tooltips share a surface (e.g. sidebar, toolbar). Prefer existing project styles (`TreeNode`, `CoverSidebar`, `AdvancedSearchSidebarTrigger`, `MdEditorToolbarTooltips`).

## Accessibility

- Icon-only triggers: keep **`aria-label`** (or visible text). Tooltip copy does not replace the accessible name.
- Do **not** add `title=` “for accessibility” alongside Radix — use `aria-label` / visible label instead.

## Nested in modals

If the tooltip opens inside a `Modal` / dialog, set Content z-index **above** the parent (baseline `z-100001` / see `modal-nested-z-index` rule).

## Out of scope

- Non-UI attributes that are not user-facing hover hints (e.g. SVG `<title>` for graphics semantics, document `<title>`).
- Confirm/dialog **titles** (`title=` prop on `ConfirmModal`, etc.) — those are dialog headings, not tooltips.

```text
❌ BAD — <button title="저장">…</button>
❌ BAD — custom absolute div shown on mouseenter as the product tooltip
❌ BAD — tippy.js / floating-ui ad-hoc tooltip kit for app chrome
✅ GOOD — Tooltip.Provider → Root → Trigger asChild → Portal → Content (+ Arrow)
✅ GOOD — icon button: aria-label + Radix Tooltip.Content with the same hint text
```

Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.
